            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Not for these pickers, no.\r\n\r\nThere is a way for `builtin.grep()` though through `opts.pattern`. For example, to search for a word under cursor (as `*` does), execute `:Pick grep pattern=\"<cword>\"`. Making it to a mapping with `'<Cmd>Pick grep pattern=\"<cword>\"<CR>'` as right hand side is more usable.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Not for these pickers, no.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">There is a way for <code class=\"notranslate\">builtin.grep()</code> though through <code class=\"notranslate\">opts.pattern</code>. For example, to search for a word under cursor (as <code class=\"notranslate\">*</code> does), execute <code class=\"notranslate\">:Pick grep pattern=\"&lt;cword&gt;\"</code>. Making it to a mapping with <code class=\"notranslate\">'&lt;Cmd&gt;Pick grep pattern=\"&lt;cword&gt;\"&lt;CR&gt;'</code> as right hand side is more usable.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Not for these pickers, no.\nThere is a way for builtin.grep() though through opts.pattern. For example, to search for a word under cursor (as * does), execute :Pick grep pattern=\"<cword>\". Making it to a mapping with '<Cmd>Pick grep pattern=\"<cword>\"<CR>' as right hand side is more usable.",
